{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"TAO","id":"267178019196633099","is_bot":0,"username":"dm_tao"},"author_id":"267178019196633099","channel_id":"863311533328695367","content":"\"*Over in Killarney \nMany years ago,  \nMe Mither sang a song to me\nIn tones so sweet and low.  \n\nJust a simple little ditty,  \nIn her good ould Irish way,  \nAnd l'd give the world if she could sing  \nThat song to me this day.   \n\n\"Too-ra-loo-ra-loo-ral, Too-ra-loo-ra-li,  Too-ra-loo-ra-loo-ral, hush now, don't you cry!  Too-ra-loo-ra-loo-ral, Too-ra-loo-ra-li,  Too-ra-loo-ra-loo-ral, that's an Irish lullaby.\"   \n\nOft in dreams I wander  \nTo that cot again,  \nI feel her arms a-huggin' me  \nAs when she held me then.  \nAnd I hear her voice a -hummin'  \nTo me as in days of yore,  \nWhen she used to rock me fast asleep  \nOutside the cabin door.*\"","created_at":"2021-07-17T19:53:43.163000Z","edited_at":"2021-07-17T19:53:55.925000Z","id":"866045020239036477","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
